@startuml
title Course Registration — Domain Class Diagram

class Student {
  +studentId: UUID
  +name: String
  +isAuthorized: Boolean
}

class Course {
  +courseCode: String
  +title: String
}

class CourseOffering {
  +offeringId: UUID
  +semester: String
  +capacity: Integer
  +enrolledCount: Integer
  +availablePlaces(): Integer
}

class Enrollment {
  +enrollmentId: UUID
  +createdAt: DateTime
}

Course "1" -- "0..*" CourseOffering : offered as
CourseOffering "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : has
Student "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : makes

note right of CourseOffering
Constraints:
capacity >= 0
0 <= enrolledCount <= capacity

availablePlaces =
capacity - enrolledCount

Invariant:
enrolledCount =
number of Enrollment records
for this offering

Enrollment creation and enrolledCount
update must commit or roll back together.
end note

note bottom of Enrollment
Uniqueness constraint:
UNIQUE(studentId, offeringId)

Each enrollment belongs to
exactly one student and one offering.
end note

note bottom of CourseOffering
A CourseOffering identifies a course
in a particular semester.

Concurrent registrations must preserve
the capacity and count invariants.
end note

@enduml
